 Implementation Plan: Add Nutanix Provider to Forklift

 Overview

 Add Nutanix AHV as a supported provider for Forklift, enabling VM migration from Nutanix infrastructure to OpenShift KubeVirt. This plan follows a
 phased approach starting with research/proof-of-concept, with clear paths to full production implementation.

 Target: Prism Central v3 API (primary), with Prism Element support (fallback)
 Approach: Phased implementation - POC first, then full migration support
 Pattern: Follow existing vSphere provider implementation as reference

 ---
 Architecture Decision: Prism Central vs Prism Element

 Primary Target: Prism Central
 - Centralized multi-cluster management (like vCenter for VMware)
 - Most enterprise deployments use Prism Central
 - Unified v3 REST API across all Nutanix clusters
 - Simpler for users with multiple clusters

 Secondary Support: Prism Element
 - Direct cluster-level management
 - Support for single-cluster deployments
 - Same v3 API structure but cluster-scoped
 - Configure via provider settings

 Implementation: Use prismType setting to differentiate, defaulting to Prism Central.

 ---
 Phase 1: Core Provider Infrastructure (POC - Week 1-2)

 Goal

 Establish basic provider registration, authentication, and inventory collection. No migration support yet.

