 ---
 Success Criteria

 POC Success (Phases 1-3)

 - Nutanix provider type registered in forklift
 - Can create Nutanix Provider CR successfully
 - Authentication with Prism Central works
 - Inventory collection completes (clusters, hosts, VMs, networks, storage)
 - REST API endpoints return Nutanix resources
 - Watch functionality works for VMs
 - UI can display Nutanix providers and inventory

 Migration Success (Phase 4)

 - Can create migration plan with Nutanix as source
 - Network mapping UI works
 - Storage mapping UI works
 - Can migrate a simple Linux VM successfully
 - Migrated VM boots in KubeVirt
 - Migrated VM retains network configuration
 - Migrated VM retains all disks

 ---
 Next Steps

 Immediate (For POC)

 1. Set up Nutanix CE test environment or use Test Drive
 2. Test Nutanix v3 API with curl/Postman to understand responses
 3. Begin Phase 1 implementation (provider type and models)
 4. Create mock test data from real Nutanix API responses

 Future (For Production)

 1. Complete migration adapter implementation
 2. Extensive testing with various VM configurations
 3. Performance optimization for large-scale migrations
 4. Documentation and user guides
 5. Console plugin UI updates (if needed)
 6. Contribute to upstream forklift project

